README.md:69:Local ports default to web 5173, API 3000, PostgreSQL 5432, and Redis 6379, bound to loopback. Set `WEB_PORT`, `API_PORT`, `DB_PORT`, `REDIS_PORT` and use `docker compose -p <isolated-name>` to avoid conflicts. The named `postgres_data` volume persists across stops. Never use `down --volumes` without explicit authorization. Source mounts enable development reload; dependency changes require rebuilds. Compose waits for PostgreSQL and Redis readiness and API health before starting dependent services; health checks retry transient startup failures. The actor endpoint requires the initial migration and a seeded admin.
README.md:71:## Redis cache
README.md:73:Redis is disposable cache storage: snapshots and AOF are disabled, `/data` uses tmpfs, and no Redis data volume is created. The server uses a 128 MB `maxmemory` limit with `allkeys-lru` eviction and a 256 MB container limit for overhead. Values may be evicted before TTL or lost on restart; authoritative data belongs in PostgreSQL. See [Redis eviction documentation](https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/reference/eviction/).
README.md:75:Host development uses `REDIS_URL`; containers use `COMPOSE_REDIS_URL` with hostname `redis`. Defaults in `.env.example` are local-only. If changing `REDIS_PASSWORD`, update both URLs with URI-encoded credentials. Production requires matching `PRODUCTION_REDIS_PASSWORD` and `PRODUCTION_REDIS_URL`, with no default password or host port. `rediss://` is supported for an external TLS-enabled Redis endpoint; the bundled Redis server uses plain Redis on its internal network.
README.md:79:Connections are lazy, shared across concurrent operations, and destroyed when the Nest application closes. Connection/handshake and command waits are each bounded at 500 ms. Offline command queuing and automatic reconnect loops are disabled; a later operation reconnects after a lost connection. A failed read returns `null`; failed writes/deletes return `false`, so callers can fall back to their data source. Invalid TTLs throw. Cache failures are handled without logging keys, payloads, URLs, or credentials. `/api/health` remains a process health check and does not establish Redis connectivity.
README.md:81:`npm test` includes cache outage and Redis URL validation checks without requiring Redis. Run the Redis integration suite against a local or isolated test instance:
